-- Conformance: every element of an array literal has the literal's element
-- type (Chapter 4, Section 4.12.1).
-- Tests: E162 — the element type is the type of the literal's first element,
-- and an element of another type is refused where it is written.  Here the
-- literal's first element is a String and its second a Nat.  Previously the
-- other elements were never compared with the first (#1584): this passed
-- check, and code generation then wrote a module that failed to load.
public fn main(@Unit -> @Nat)
  requires(true)
  ensures(true)
  effects(pure)
{
  array_length(["a", 5])
}
